NOTE ON DATA — the MIT licence above covers this SOURCE CODE only.

It grants you nothing with respect to the data the software fetches. Each
upstream source carries its own terms, and some of them restrict exactly the
uses this licence would otherwise permit:

  * Congressional financial disclosures — 5 U.S.C. §13107(c)(1)(B) makes it
    unlawful to obtain or use these reports "for any commercial purpose"
    (news and communications media excepted), with civil penalties to $10,000.
    Free, open-source, self-hosted personal research is fine. A paid product
    must not include that lane.

  * FINRA — Terms of Use permit "ONLY your own non-commercial personal or
    professional use", and restriction (d) forbids developing or creating a
    database from FINRA website data. This source is disabled by default;
    enabling it is your decision, made against the terms reproduced in the UI.

  * Cboe — delayed options quotes carry OPRA data. Showing OPRA data
    externally in an app, tool, or website makes you a redistributor
    (US$1,500/month), with no exemption for free, open-source, or
    non-commercial use. Run this software locally; do not host it publicly.

  * SEC EDGAR, U.S. Treasury, CFTC — U.S. government works; commercial use
    and redistribution are unrestricted. EDGAR asks for a request rate under
    10/second and a User-Agent identifying the caller.

Complying with those terms, in your jurisdiction and for your use case, is
your responsibility and not the author's.
